---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
const BARS = 24;
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Switch a flag off for 20,000 servers" hint="You turn off a broken feature with a kill switch, and 10 seconds later the flag service goes down. Choose how the SDKs get the change and watch how long users keep seeing the old value. A second change, a rollout rising from 10% to 30%, shows what sticky bucketing protects.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The defaults (<b>polling every 60 s, a 5-minute outage, cold starts fail closed</b>): only the SDKs that polled in the first 10 seconds get the kill switch. The rest <b>keep the broken feature on for 5 to 6 minutes</b>, and the fleet serves it to about <b>53 million requests</b>.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>streaming</b>: the change reaches every connected SDK in <b>under a second</b>, before the outage starts, and the stale requests drop to about <b>0.1 million</b>. The price is 20,000 open connections and a <b>reconnect storm of about 4,000 requests per second</b> when the service returns.</li>
    <li>Pick <b>polling a CDN copy</b> and set the outage to <b>none</b>: the service load falls from about <b>333 to under 1 request per second</b>, but the change is slower, because it waits for the cache to expire <b>and</b> for the next poll. Then go back to a 5-minute outage with <b>polling the flag service</b> and compare the three <b>cold-start</b> choices: fail closed hides healthy features and fail open shows unfinished ones (each about 3.2 million requests), and a bundled ruleset avoids both, though its copy still has the old value of the kill switch.</li>
    <li>Change the <b>bucketing</b> to random on every request: about <b>185 users lose a feature they already had</b> when the rollout rises, and most users flicker. With a hash of user and flag, nobody loses it.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg ffb" data-ffb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>SDKs get the change by <select class="pg-in" data-mode>
        <option value="poll" selected>polling the flag service</option>
        <option value="cdn">polling a CDN copy</option>
        <option value="stream">streaming (SSE) from the service</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Poll interval <select class="pg-in" data-p>
        <option value="5">5 s</option><option value="15">15 s</option><option value="30">30 s</option>
        <option value="60" selected>60 s</option><option value="120">2 min</option><option value="300">5 min</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>CDN cache lifetime <select class="pg-in" data-t>
        <option value="5">5 s</option><option value="15">15 s</option><option value="30">30 s</option>
        <option value="60" selected>60 s</option><option value="300">5 min</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Flag service outage <select class="pg-in" data-out>
        <option value="0">none</option><option value="1">1 minute</option>
        <option value="5" selected>5 minutes</option><option value="30">30 minutes</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>An SDK that starts with no ruleset <select class="pg-in" data-cold>
        <option value="closed" selected>fails closed (every flag off)</option>
        <option value="open">fails open (every flag on)</option>
        <option value="bundled">uses a ruleset bundled in the image</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Rollout buckets users by <select class="pg-in" data-bk>
        <option value="sticky" selected>hash of user id and this flag's salt</option>
        <option value="shared">hash of user id, one salt for all flags</option>
        <option value="random">a random number on every request</option>
        <option value="resalt">hash, with a new salt when the percentage changes</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="chart" aria-hidden="true" data-chart>
      {Array.from({ length: BARS }, () => <span class="bar"></span>)}
    </div>
    <p class="axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>0 s</span><span data-axis>share of the fleet that has switched the feature off, over time</span><span data-max></span></p>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Time until the feature is off</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Requests served the broken feature</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Load on the flag service</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>SDKs that restart during the outage</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>Rollout rises from 10% to 30%</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 20,000 SDK instances, each handling 10 requests per second, and 50 CDN edge caches. At second 0 the kill switch is published. The service goes down at second 10 and stays down for the chosen time. Polls start at random moments within the interval. A CDN edge refreshes when its copy expires, can not refresh while the service is down, and keeps serving the old copy meanwhile. Streaming SDKs get a push about half a second after the change, and reconnect within 5 seconds after an outage. 5% of the instances restart at second 10 with no cached ruleset; behind a CDN they read the edge copy, otherwise they use the chosen fallback until the service returns. The rollout uses 3,000 simulated users, each making 12 requests to random instances while the change spreads.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style>
  .chart { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: 2px; height: 110px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .bar { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; background: var(--accent); opacity: .75; border-radius: 1px 1px 0 0; height: 2%; transition: height .25s; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .bar { transition: none; } }
  .axis { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px; margin: 4px 2px 10px; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
<script>
  import { query } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ffb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const N = 20000; const EDGES = 50; const RATE = 10; const DOWN_AT = 10; const COLD_EVERY = 20; const USERS = 3000; const REQS = 12; const BARS = 24;
    const SEC_PER_MIN = 60;
    const APPLY_S = { poll: 0.1, cdn: 0.3, cdnCold: 0.2, streamMin: 0.2, streamRange: 0.6 }; // time from receiving a ruleset to using it
    const RECONNECT_JITTER_S = 5; // streaming clients reconnect within 5 s of the service returning
    const COLD_RETRY_MAX_S = 30; // a cold SDK retries at most every 30 s
    const ROLLOUT = { before: 0.1, after: 0.3 }; // the rollout goes from 10% to 30%
    const ROLLOUT_MIN_WINDOW_S = 3; // users' requests are spread over at least 3 s
    const BAR_MIN_PCT = 2;
    const WARN = { killS: 30, reqs: 5e6, pollRps: 1000, stormRps: 2000, flickPct: 10, fastPollS: 15 }; // card and verdict thresholds
    // Numerical Recipes LCG
    let seed = 77; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const arr = (n: number) => Array.from({ length: n }, rnd);
    const U = arr(N); const CU = arr(N); const D = arr(N); const CJ = arr(N); const UE = arr(EDGES);
    const B1 = arr(USERS); const B2 = arr(USERS); const BO = arr(USERS); const BR = arr(USERS); const AR = arr(USERS);
    const UT = Array.from({ length: USERS }, () => arr(REQS)); const UI = Array.from({ length: USERS }, () => arr(REQS)); const UR = Array.from({ length: USERS }, () => arr(REQS));
    const bars = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.bar'));
    const fmtN = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const fmtM = (n: number) => (n >= 1e5 ? `${(n / 1e6).toFixed(1)} million` : `${fmtN(n)}`);
    const dur = (s: number) => (s < 1 ? 'under 1 s' : s < 120 ? `${s.toFixed(s < 10 ? 1 : 0)} s` : s < 7200 ? `${(s / 60).toFixed(1)} min` : `${(s / 3600).toFixed(1)} h`);
    function simulate(mode: string, P: number, T: number, outMin: number, cold: string, bucketing: string) {
      const up = DOWN_AT + outMin * SEC_PER_MIN; // the moment the service is back (equal to the failure time when there is no outage)
      const inOut = (t: number) => outMin > 0 && t >= DOWN_AT && t < up;
      const skip = (t: number) => (inOut(t) ? t + P * Math.ceil((up - t) / P) : t); // a failed poll is simply tried again one interval later
      const avail = UE.map((u) => { const a = u * T; return inOut(a) ? up + 1 : a; }); // when each edge cache gets the new ruleset
      const tNew = new Array<number>(N); const tOff = new Array<number>(N); const hits = new Map<number, number>();
      const hit = (t: number) => { const k = Math.floor(t); hits.set(k, (hits.get(k) ?? 0) + 1); };
      let onSec = 0; let wrongSec = 0;
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        const phi = U[i] * P; let t: number;
        if (mode === 'poll') { t = skip(phi) + APPLY_S.poll; hit(phi + P * Math.ceil((up - phi) / P)); }
        else if (mode === 'cdn') { const a = avail[i % EDGES]; t = phi; if (t < a) t += P * Math.ceil((a - t) / P); t += APPLY_S.cdn; }
        else { t = APPLY_S.streamMin + D[i] * APPLY_S.streamRange; if (outMin > 0) hit(up + CJ[i] * RECONNECT_JITTER_S); }
        tNew[i] = t; tOff[i] = t; onSec += t;
      }
      if (mode === 'cdn') for (let e = 0; e < EDGES; e++) hit(avail[e]);
      let coldCount = 0;
      if (outMin > 0) for (let i = 0; i < N; i += COLD_EVERY) {
        coldCount++; const warmOn = Math.min(tNew[i], DOWN_AT); onSec += warmOn - tNew[i];
        if (mode === 'cdn') {
          const a = avail[i % EDGES]; let t = DOWN_AT + APPLY_S.cdnCold;
          if (a > DOWN_AT) { const phi = DOWN_AT + CU[i] * P; t = phi + P * Math.max(0, Math.ceil((a - phi) / P)) + APPLY_S.cdn; }
          onSec += t - DOWN_AT; tOff[i] = t;
        } else {
          const ready = up + (mode === 'stream' ? CJ[i] * RECONNECT_JITTER_S : CU[i] * Math.min(P, COLD_RETRY_MAX_S)); hit(ready);
          if (cold === 'closed') { wrongSec += ready - DOWN_AT; tOff[i] = warmOn; }
          else if (cold === 'open') { wrongSec += ready - DOWN_AT; onSec += ready - DOWN_AT; tOff[i] = ready; }
          else { onSec += ready - DOWN_AT; tOff[i] = ready; }
        }
      }
      const sorted = [...tOff].sort((a, b) => a - b); const at = (p: number) => sorted[Math.min(N - 1, Math.ceil(p * N) - 1)];
      let peak = 0; hits.forEach((v) => { if (v > peak) peak = v; });
      const steady = mode === 'poll' ? N / P : mode === 'cdn' ? Math.min(EDGES / T, N / P) : 0;
      // The rollout: the same propagation, seen by simulated users who hit random instances.
      const sw = [...tNew].sort((a, b) => a - b); const W = Math.max(sw[Math.ceil(0.99 * N) - 1], ROLLOUT_MIN_WINDOW_S);
      let lost = 0; let flick = 0; let overlapN = 0; let overlapD = 0;
      for (let u = 0; u < USERS; u++) {
        const ev = (fresh: boolean, r: number) => (bucketing === 'random' ? r < (fresh ? ROLLOUT.after : ROLLOUT.before) : bucketing === 'resalt' ? (fresh ? B2[u] < ROLLOUT.after : B1[u] < ROLLOUT.before) : B1[u] < (fresh ? ROLLOUT.after : ROLLOUT.before));
        const before = ev(false, BR[u]); const after = ev(true, AR[u]);
        if (before && !after) lost++;
        if (after) { overlapD++; if (bucketing === 'shared' ? B1[u] < ROLLOUT.after : BO[u] < ROLLOUT.after) overlapN++; }
        const reqs = UT[u].map((f, k) => ({ t: f * W, i: Math.floor(UI[u][k] * N), r: UR[u][k] })).sort((a, b) => a.t - b.t);
        let prev: boolean | null = null; let fl = false;
        for (const x of reqs) { const on = ev(x.t >= tNew[x.i], x.r); if (prev === true && on === false) fl = true; prev = on; }
        if (fl) flick++;
      }
      return { p50: at(0.5), p99: at(0.99), max: sorted[N - 1], steady, peak, req: onSec * RATE, wrong: wrongSec * RATE, coldCount, lost, flick, overlap: overlapN / Math.max(1, overlapD), up, sorted };
    }
    function draw() {
      const mode = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mode]').value; const P = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-p]').value); const T = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-t]').value);
      const outMin = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-out]').value); const cold = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cold]').value; const bk = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-bk]').value;
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-p]').disabled = mode === 'stream'; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-t]').disabled = mode !== 'cdn'; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cold]').disabled = mode === 'cdn' || outMin === 0;
      const r = simulate(mode, P, T, outMin, cold, bk);
      // cumulative share of instances that no longer serve the broken feature
      const max = Math.max(r.max, 1);
      let j = 0; bars.forEach((b, k) => { const x = (max * (k + 1)) / BARS; while (j < N && r.sorted[j] <= x) j++; b.style.height = `${Math.max(BAR_MIN_PCT, (j / N) * 100)}%`; });
      q('[data-max]').textContent = dur(max);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `half: ${dur(r.p50)}, 99%: ${dur(r.p99)}`; q('[data-n1]').textContent = `the last instance: ${dur(r.max)}`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = fmtM(r.req); q('[data-n2]').textContent = `${fmtN(N)} instances at ${RATE} requests per second each, counted until each one switches`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = mode === 'stream' ? `${fmtN(N)} open connections` : `${r.steady < 10 ? r.steady.toFixed(1) : fmtN(r.steady)} requests per second`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = mode === 'stream' ? (outMin > 0 ? `reconnect storm after the outage: ${fmtN(r.peak)} requests per second` : `one push of ${fmtN(N)} messages for the change`) : `busiest second after the change: ${fmtN(r.peak)}${mode === 'cdn' ? ' (the cache keeps the SDKs off the service)' : ''}`;
      if (outMin === 0) { q('[data-o4]').textContent = 'no outage'; q('[data-n4]').textContent = 'a new SDK simply fetches the ruleset'; }
      else if (mode === 'cdn') { q('[data-o4]').textContent = `${fmtN(r.coldCount)} read the CDN copy`; q('[data-n4]').textContent = 'the CDN keeps serving a ruleset while the service is down'; }
      else {
        q('[data-o4]').textContent = cold === 'closed' ? `${fmtM(r.wrong)} requests with healthy features off` : cold === 'open' ? `${fmtM(r.wrong)} requests with unfinished features on` : 'no wrong values';
        q('[data-n4]').textContent = `${fmtN(r.coldCount)} instances, until the service returns` + (cold === 'bundled' ? '; the bundled ruleset still has the old value of the kill switch' : cold === 'open' ? '; and the killed feature is on again' : '');
      }
      const lostPct = (r.lost / USERS) * 100; const flickPct = (r.flick / USERS) * 100;
      q('[data-o5]').textContent = `${fmtN(r.lost)} of ${fmtN(USERS)} users lose it`; q('[data-n5]').textContent = `${flickPct.toFixed(0)}% see it go back off during the spread; ${(r.overlap * 100).toFixed(0)}% of them also have another 30% flag`;
      const bad = (el: string, v: boolean) => q<HTMLElement>(el).style.setProperty('--c', v ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      bad('[data-b1]', r.p99 > WARN.killS); bad('[data-b2]', r.req > WARN.reqs); bad('[data-b3]', (mode === 'poll' && r.steady > WARN.pollRps) || (mode === 'stream' && outMin > 0 && r.peak > WARN.stormRps)); bad('[data-b4]', (mode !== 'cdn' && outMin > 0 && cold !== 'bundled')); bad('[data-b5]', r.lost > 0 || flickPct > WARN.flickPct);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]');
      const msgs: string[] = [];
      if (r.p99 > WARN.killS) msgs.push(`The kill switch took ${dur(r.p99)} to reach 99% of the fleet, and the broken feature answered ${fmtM(r.req)} requests meanwhile${outMin > 0 && mode !== 'stream' ? `, because the outage stopped the polls that came after second ${DOWN_AT}` : ''}.`);
      else msgs.push(`The kill switch reached 99% of the fleet in ${dur(r.p99)}.`);
      if (mode === 'stream' && outMin > 0) msgs.push(`Streaming delivered the change before the service failed, but the return of the service brought ${fmtN(r.peak)} reconnects in one second.`);
      if (mode === 'poll' && P <= WARN.fastPollS) msgs.push(`Polling every ${P} s costs the service ${fmtN(r.steady)} requests per second all the time.`);
      if (bk === 'random' || bk === 'resalt') msgs.push(`Without a stable hash, ${fmtN(r.lost)} users lost a feature they had (${lostPct.toFixed(0)}%).`);
      else if (bk === 'shared') msgs.push('A shared salt never takes anyone back, but the same users land in every rollout, so the other flag overlaps 100% and experiments are biased.');
      else msgs.push(`With a stable hash nobody loses the feature, but ${flickPct.toFixed(0)}% of users still saw it switch off while instances disagreed.`);
      out.textContent = msgs.join(' '); out.classList.toggle('bad', r.p99 > WARN.killS || r.lost > 0);
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
